                                <fo:block-container space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">Here you will
                                        learn what is subtraction</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">Subtraction is the
                                        process of finding the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">difference between two
                                            numbers</fo:inline> by taking one number away from another. </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">When using a
                                        calculator, you <fo:inline font-weight="bold">enter the
                                            first number</fo:inline>, <fo:inline font-weight="bold">press the minus (–)</fo:inline>
                                        button, <fo:inline font-weight="bold">enter the
                                            second number</fo:inline>, <fo:inline font-weight="bold">then press equals (=)</fo:inline> to
                                        get the result.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"> It shows how much
                                        remains after removing one value from another.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                            </fo:block>
